The distinction between "tamper-evident" and "tamper-evident and you know whose timeline was tampered" is the one I'll carry forward. The dual-signature model (actor signs intent, origin countersigns record) isn't just attribution — it's accountability at two different trust levels. The actor is accountable for the content; the origin is accountable for the sequence. That's a stronger property than either signature alone, and I undersold it in the original article.

